^XPD(9.6,13458,0)="PSO*7.0*724^60^0^3230601^y"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,0)="^^49^49^3230526^"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,3,0)="1) Zero Report email verbiage:"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,4,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,5,0)="When the Scheduled SPMP Data Export [PSO SPMP SCHEDULED EXPORT] job fails"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,6,0)="to transmit a Zero Report batch, two emails for the Zero Report"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,7,0)="batch are generated with contradicting wording.  First sent is an email "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,8,0)="saying the transmission failed; then a second email is sent saying that "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,9,0)="the Zero Report was transmitted.  To reduce confusion at the sites, the "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,10,0)="wording in the Zero Report should be corrected to not indicate the "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,11,0)="transmission status, thereby avoiding contradicting with the preceding "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,12,0)="""transmission failed"" email. "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,13,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,14,0)="2) PSO*7*696 IOC follow-up issues:"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,15,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,16,0)="Four issues were identified regarding the new SPMP State Parameter for "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,17,0)="ZERO REPORT DEFAULT DIVISON during IOC for previous patch PSO*7*696."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,18,0)="All of the items deal with the View/Edit SPMP State Parameters option"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,19,0)="[PSO SPMP STATE PARAMETERS]."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,20,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,21,0)="    1.  When the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER=""2"" but the ZERO REPORT "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,22,0)="    DEFAULT DIVISION State Parameter is not set, then no Zero Report "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,23,0)="    is generated. However, currently the ZERO REPORT DEFAULT DIVISION is"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,24,0)="    not a required field when using the View/Edit SPMP State Parameters"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,25,0)="    option [PSO SPMP STATE PARAMETERS]. It should be made required "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,26,0)="    within the View/Edit SPMP State Parameters option [PSO SPMP STATE"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,27,0)="    PARAMETERS] for SEND=2 to ensure that Zero reports will be sent."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,28,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,29,0)="    2.  The Help Text for the ZERO REPORT DEFAULT DIVISION State "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,30,0)="    Parameter does not clearly indicate it is required when the "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,31,0)="    SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER=""2"".  "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,32,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,33,0)="    3.  When using the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER, the State Parameter "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,34,0)="    ZERO REPORT DEFAULT DIVISION shows ""//"" even when it's blank.  "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,35,0)="    This is not normal behavior since empty fields should not have ""//""."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,36,0)="    This is only cosmetic and does not affect functionality of the"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,37,0)="    Zero Report, but it should be fixed."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,38,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,39,0)="    4.  The Technical Description of the ZERO REPORT DEFAULT DIVISION "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,40,0)="    State Parameter wording is a little confusing by saying it's used"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,41,0)="    for ""MbM states that do not  dispense controlled substances""."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,42,0)="    It should be clarified to say this is used when a state has"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,43,0)="    State Parameter SEND  EXPORT STATE PARAMETER=2."
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,44,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,45,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,46,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,47,0)="---------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,48,0)="INC26586596 - Zero Report verbiage"
^XPD(9.6,13458,1,49,0)="INC27015594 - PSO*7*696 IOC follow-up issues"
^XPD(9.6,13458,4,0)="^9.64PA^58.41^1"
^XPD(9.6,13458,4,58.41,0)=58.41
^XPD(9.6,13458,4,58.41,2,0)="^9.641^58.41^1"
^XPD(9.6,13458,4,58.41,2,58.41,0)="SPMP STATE PARAMETERS  (File-top level)"
