^XPD(9.6,13459,0)="PSO*7.0*728^60^0^3230807^y"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,0)="^^23^23^3230626^"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,1,0)="When processing a OneVA fill (refill or partial), the user is prompted for"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,2,0)="a label device. After device selection, the software will first send the"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,3,0)="fill to the Outpatient Pharmacy Automated Interface (OPAI), if applicable,"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,4,0)="then attempt to print a label. But if the user selected a device that is"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,5,0)="not designated as a laser label device, an error occurs when the label "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,6,0)="prints because only laser labels can print for a OneVA fill. And the user"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,7,0)="will get a View Alert regarding this error. The resolution if a non"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,8,0)="laser label device was selected is to not make the attempt to print the"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,9,0)="label, so no error will be logged in the error trap and the user will not"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,10,0)="get a View Alert. If a laser label device is selected at the label prompt,"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,11,0)="the laser label will still print without issues."
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,12,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,13,0)="When sending a OneVA fill (refill or partial) to the OPAI, the routing"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,14,0)="(WINDOW or MAIL) is based on previous routing information for the"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,15,0)="prescription from the Host Site. This patch will now set the routing to"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,16,0)="WINDOW for all OneVA fills."
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,17,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,18,0)="When a OneVA fill is processed and sent to the OPAI, filling information "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,19,0)="is sent from the dispensing site back to host site in an HL7 message. The "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,20,0)="problem is even if the message was successful, the VistA HL7 message will "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,21,0)="display a Status of ""ERROR"", and an Err Type of ""Message was NAK'ed"". "
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,22,0)="This patch resolves the issue so these messages will now show as"
^XPD(9.6,13459,1,23,0)="successfully transmitted."
^XPD(9.6,13459,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
