^XPD(9.6,13485,0)="FH*5.5*55^9^0^3230104^y"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,0)="^^94^94^3220706^"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,3,0)="ALERT FOR WRONG PATIENT DISPLAYS WHEN ACCESSING VIEW ALERTS "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,4,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,5,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,6,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,7,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,8,0)="====================="
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,9,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,10,0)="1.      INC22357619- ALERT FOR WRONG PATIENT DISPLAYS WHEN ACCESSING VIEW "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,11,0)="ALERTS"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,12,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,13,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,14,0)="=================="
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,15,0)="N/A"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,16,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,17,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,18,0)="========================="
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,19,0)="TBD"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,20,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,21,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,22,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,23,0)="==========================================="
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,24,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,25,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,26,0)="1. INC22357619 - ALERT FOR WRONG PATIENT DISPLAYS IN VIEW ALERTS"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,27,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,28,0)="   Problem:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,29,0)="   -------"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,30,0)="Alert for wrong patient displayed when accessing View Alerts and an alert "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,31,0)="displayed for a different patient when using View Alert.  This issue was "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,32,0)="reviewed by the Kernel team and their findings were that the application "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,33,0)="is creating an incorrect Package identifier (four comma pieces instead of "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,34,0)="three), so that when the application processes the alert, the patient id "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,35,0)="or notification id are incorrectly referenced. This was found to be due "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,36,0)="to the Package identifier being created using $H which itself contains a "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,37,0)="comma."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,38,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,39,0)="   Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,40,0)="   ----------"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,41,0)="The use of $H to create the Package identifier does allow the creation of "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,42,0)="a unique identifier but causes problems due to the extra comma.  This "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,43,0)="patch will modify FH routines to modify the package id sent to kernel to "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,44,0)="conform with kernel documentation.  Kernel 8.0 & Kernel Toolkit 7.3"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,45,0)="Developer's Guide documents the package id as follows:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,46,0)="Paragraph 3.2.1 - The software application identifier for an alert is "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,47,0)="defined as the original value of the XQAID input variable when the alert "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,48,0)="is created via the SETUP^XQALERT: Send Alerts API. Typically, the "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,49,0)="software application identifier should begin with the software "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,50,0)="application namespace."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,51,0)="Paragraph 3.3 - The Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) software "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,52,0)="uses a convention for the format of the software application identifier "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,53,0)="consisting of three comma-delimited pieces:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,54,0)="namespace_"",""_dfn_"",""_notificationcode"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,55,0)="Where:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,56,0)="   - namespace is the software application namespace."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,57,0)="   - dfn is the internal entry number of the patient whom the alert "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,58,0)="     concerns in the PATIENT (#2) file."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,59,0)="   - notificationcode is a code maintained by the CPRS software "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,60,0)="     describing the type of alert."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,61,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,62,0)="Prior to this patch the XQAID variable passed to kernel was created as "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,63,0)="""FH,""_$J_"",""_$H ($J is the vista job# for the task & $H is mumps "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,64,0)="date/time)"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,65,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,66,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,67,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,68,0)="   --------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,69,0)="The setting of XQAID in routines ALRT^FHCTF5, ALRT^FHASM2A, PHA^FHASM2A "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,70,0)="and FIL^FHWTRN is changed to use the patient's DFN as the 2nd comma piece "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,71,0)="and a number identifying the FH alert type in the 3rd piece."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,72,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,73,0)="""FH,""_DFN_"",""_TYPE"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,74,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,75,0)="The types are as follows"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,76,0)="1 = Food/drug interaction alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,77,0)="2 = Nutrition Patient assessment alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,78,0)="3 = Monitor BMI alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,79,0)="4 = Monitor Tubefeed alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,80,0)="5 = Monitor Hyperals alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,81,0)="6 = Monitor Albumin alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,82,0)="7 = Monitor NPO+Clr alert"
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,83,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,84,0)="The TYPE is set into the variable FHCODE in routines FHWTRN & FHCTF5 for "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,85,0)="each type of alert."
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,86,0)="During analysis it was also found that routines FHWTRN & FHCTF5 were "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,87,0)="passing in FHCTF2 as the entry point for processing the alert but did not "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,88,0)="include a routine name for processing, therefore the alert is deleted "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,89,0)="which I believe is correct because these alerts I believe are meant to be "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,90,0)="informational.  Setting an entry point should not have been done and both "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,91,0)="entry point and routine should not be set. "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,92,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,93,0)="This patch comments out the code S XQAOPT=""FHCTF2"" at FIL+11^FHWTRN and "
^XPD(9.6,13485,1,94,0)="ALRT+9^FHCTF5."
^XPD(9.6,13485,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
^XPD(9.6,13485,6)="^50"
^XPD(9.6,13485,6.3)=7
^XPD(9.6,13485,"ABPKG")="n"
^XPD(9.6,13485,"KRN",0)="^9.67PA^1.5^25"
^XPD(9.6,13485,"KRN",.4,0)=.4
