^XPD(9.6,13541,0)="PSO*7.0*712^60^0^3231004^y"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,0)="^^18^18^3230511^"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,3,0)="With the introduction of PARK functionality (CPRS 32B release), and"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,4,0)="once the Park functionality is enabled, the Health Summary Type of"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,5,0)="Essential Med List for Review needs to be able to display ""Active/Parked"""
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,6,0)="as a status. The Application Program Interface (API), PSO52API, which"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,7,0)="provides the prescription details for this report has been modified to"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,8,0)="return a status of ACTIVE/PARKED if the calling package is HEALTH"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,9,0)="SUMMARY (GMTS). Along with changes in patch GMTS*2.7*145, the Essential"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,10,0)="Med List for Review will now be able to display ""Active/Parked"""
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,11,0)="when the prescription is in a Parked status."
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,12,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,13,0)="This patch also modifies the logic related to refilling a Parked"
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,14,0)="Prescription. If the original fill or the refill is not released, or "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,15,0)="label not printed or not processed by CMOP then that fill will be "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,16,0)="processed, and the prescription will be placed in suspended status. "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,17,0)="Otherwise, the current logic in refilling the prescription will be "
^XPD(9.6,13541,1,18,0)="followed."
^XPD(9.6,13541,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
^XPD(9.6,13541,6)="10^569"
^XPD(9.6,13541,6.3)=20
