^XPD(9.6,13560,0)="PSO*7.0*700^60^0^3231114^y"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,0)="^^897^897^3231020^^^^"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,1,0)="The Inbound Electronic Prescribing (eRx) enhancements delivered in this"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,2,0)="patch include updates to the current eRx functionality to convert all"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,3,0)="of the MbM Class 3 modifications into Class 1. Below is summary of the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,4,0)="change being delivered in this patch. For a more comprehensive description of"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,5,0)="the changes please refer to the documents listed in the Documentation section"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,6,0)="of this description."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,7,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,8,0)="1. Lock Timeout Change (MbM ONLY)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,9,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,10,0)="   The LOCK timeout was intentionally changed to 0.01 seconds for MbM for the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,11,0)="   following options in order to assist MbM in the processing of high-volume"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,12,0)="   incoming eRx's:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,13,0)="      "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,14,0)="        Complete Orders from eRx [PSO ERX FINISH]"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,15,0)="        eRx Holding Queue Processing [PSO ERX QUEUE PROCESSING]"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,16,0)="        Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH]"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,17,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,18,0)="2. eRx Provider Auto-Validation (MbM ONLY)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,19,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,20,0)="   a) A new logic for auto-validating a VistA Providers for MbM sites is being"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,21,0)="      added by this patch to assist MbM in the processing of high-volume"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,22,0)="      incoming eRx's. In order to auto-validate a provider the following "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,23,0)="      conditions must be fulfilled:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,24,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,25,0)="      - eRx Providers was auto-matched to a VistA Provider"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,26,0)="      - eRx Provider last name matches VistA Provider last name"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,27,0)="      - First letter of eRx Provider first name matches first letter of VistA"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,28,0)="        Provider first name"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,29,0)="      - Zip code for the eRx Provider matches the zip code for the VistA"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,30,0)="        Provider"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,31,0)="      - eRx is not electronically signed (CS eRx)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,32,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,33,0)="   b) The Audit Log will display ""AUTO-VALIDATED"" to indicate that a provider"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,34,0)="      was auto-validated, as seen in the example below:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,35,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,36,0)="        New Value: PROVIDER,NAME(DEA#: AX1212543) - AUTO-VALIDATED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,37,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,38,0)="   c) The Single Patient list will identify such event (auto-validation) by"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,39,0)="      by highlighting the letter ""V"" under the MATCHING/PR column."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,40,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,41,0)="3. VistA Patient and VistA Provider Look-up (MbM ONLY)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,42,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,43,0)="   The VistA Patient and Provider lookup prompts have been modified to display"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,44,0)="   different information for MbM sites only:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,45,0)="   - For the VistA Patient it displays:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,46,0)="       Name, DOB, SSN, City and State"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,47,0)="       (e.g., AAQDY,BUDT LUSER 08/04/1954  101058613  PADDLETON,MD)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,48,0)="   - For the VistA Provider it displays:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,49,0)="       Name, City, State, DEA# and Exp. (if any)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,50,0)="      (e.g., AEXRFGRI,APSKACWHZ  TORRINGTON,WY DEA#: AA4729919 (Exp: 01/01/24)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,51,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,52,0)="4. VistA Patient Suggestion"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,53,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,54,0)="   When matching eRx Patient to a corresponding VistA Patient before the user"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,55,0)="   is prompted for the VistA entry it will first be presented with suggestion"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,56,0)="   (if any) based on the following logic:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,57,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,58,0)="  - Once a VistA Patient is matched and later validated to an eRx Patient it"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,59,0)="    is then ""remembered"""
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,60,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,61,0)="  - When a new eRx prescription is received for the same eRx Patient the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,62,0)="    ""remembered"" VistA Patient(s) are then presented as suggestions for the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,63,0)="    user to select, as shown below (Validate Patient Screen - Edit action):"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,64,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,65,0)="    Select Item(s): Next Screen// E   Edit  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,66,0)="                                                     |Sugg. 1 of 1 - 08/08/23|"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,67,0)="    ERX PATIENT                        VISTA PATIENT |From eRx#: 123123      |"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,68,0)="    ___________________________________________________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,69,0)="    Name:OPEKXAQDY,XUISCSD            |Name:OPEKXAQDY,XUISCSD F"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,70,0)="    DOB :DEC 18, 1970                 |DOB :DEC 18, 1970"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,71,0)="    Sex :MALE                         |Sex :MALE"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,72,0)="    SSN :101127944                    |SSN :101-13-4021"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,73,0)="    Address:                          |Address:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,74,0)="     123 FAKE STREET #101             | 123 FLAKE ST SUITE 101"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,75,0)="     PLANO,TX  75025                  | PLANO,TX 75025"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,76,0)="    Primary Phone: 0236663417         |"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,77,0)="    __________________________________|_______________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,78,0)="    ACTION on SUGGESTION: (A)CCEPT  (F)ORGET  (E)XIT: EXIT// "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,79,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,80,0)="  - The left column has information about the eRx Patient while the right"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,81,0)="    column has information about the VistA Patient. The 'Last Match' field"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,82,0)="    indicates the last time the VistA Patient was matched to the eRx Patient"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,83,0)="    and validated. When a corresponding field does not match it will display"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,84,0)="    in reverse video."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,85,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,86,0)="  - When presented with a suggestion the user is given 3 options: (A)ccept,"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,87,0)="    (F)orget or (E)xit:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,88,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,89,0)="    ACCEPT - Accepts the suggested VistA Provider and matches it to the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,90,0)="    FORGET - Forgets this suggested VistA Provider so that it is not "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,91,0)="             presented again in the future to any user"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,92,0)="    EXIT   - Exits and proceed to match the VistA Provider manually"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,93,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,94,0)="    If more than one suggestion exists, then a 4th option is included: (N)ext:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,95,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,96,0)="    ACTION on SUGGESTION: (A)CCEPT  (F)ORGET  (N)EXT  (E)XIT: EXIT// "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,97,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,98,0)="    NEXT   - Ignores the current suggestion and view the next one"" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,99,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,100,0)="5. VistA Provider Suggestion"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,101,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,102,0)="   When matching eRx Provider to a corresponding VistA Provider before the "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,103,0)="   user is prompted for the VistA entry it will first be presented with "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,104,0)="   suggestion (if any) based on the following logic:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,105,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,106,0)="  - Once a VistA Provider is matched and later validated to an eRx Provider it"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,107,0)="    is then ""remembered"""
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,108,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,109,0)="  - When a new eRx prescription is received for the same eRx Provider the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,110,0)="    ""remembered"" VistA Provider(s) are then presented as suggestions for the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,111,0)="    user to select, as shown below (Validate Patient Screen - Edit action):"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,112,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,113,0)="    Select Item(s): Next Screen// E   Edit  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,114,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,115,0)="  - Below is an example for the Provider matching (Validate Provider Screen -"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,116,0)="    Edit action):"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,117,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,118,0)="                                                      |Sugg. 1 of 1 - 08/08/23|"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,119,0)="    ERX PROVIDER                        VISTA PROVIDER|From eRx#: 123123      |"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,120,0)="    __________________________________________________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,121,0)="    Name:AEXRFGRI,APSKACWHZ            |Name:AEXRFGRI,APSKACWHZ"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,122,0)="    NPI :1144286097                    |NPI :1073579710"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,123,0)="    DEA#:AA1216680                     |DEA#:AA1216680"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,124,0)="    Phone #: 555-220-0303              |Phone #: (555) 220-0303"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,125,0)="    Address:                           |Address:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,126,0)="    123 INTERNATIONAL RD               |123 INTERNATIONAL RD"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,127,0)="    GREENVILLE, IL 66024               |GREENVILLE, IL 66024"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,128,0)="    __________________________________|_______________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,129,0)="    ACTION on SUGGESTION: (A)CCEPT  (F)ORGET  (E)XIT: EXIT// "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,130,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,131,0)="  - When presented with a suggestion the user is given 3 options: (A)ccept,"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,132,0)="    (F)orget or (E)xit:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,133,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,134,0)="    ACCEPT - Accepts the suggested VistA Provider and matches it to the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,135,0)="    FORGET - Forgets this suggested VistA Provider so that it is not "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,136,0)="             presented again in the future to any user"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,137,0)="    EXIT   - Exits and proceed to match the VistA Provider manually"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,138,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,139,0)="    If more than one suggestion exists, then a 4th option is included: (N)ext:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,140,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,141,0)="    ACTION on SUGGESTION: (A)CCEPT  (F)ORGET  (N)EXT  (E)XIT: EXIT// "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,142,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,143,0)="    NEXT   - Ignores the current suggestion and view the next one"""
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,144,0)="    "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,145,0)="6. VistA Medication (Drug, Dosage, Qty, etc...) Suggestion"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,146,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,147,0)="   When matching the eRx Drug to a corresponding VistA Drug before the "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,148,0)="   user is prompted for the VistA entry it will first be presented with "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,149,0)="   suggestion (if any) based on the following logic:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,150,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,151,0)="  - Once an eRx is accepted, it moves to the Pending Queue as a Pending Order."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,152,0)="    After the Pending Order is finished it becomes an Active prescription. At"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,153,0)="    this point the software will ""create a memory"" of how the prescription was"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,154,0)="    entered (Drug, Dosage, Days Supply, Qty, # of refills, etc). "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,155,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,156,0)="  - When a new eRx prescription is received for the same eRx Drug, NDC"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,157,0)="    Code, SIG, Qty, Days Supply, # of Refills and Substitution allowance. the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,158,0)="    ""remembered"" VistA fields are then presented as suggestions for the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,159,0)="    user to select, as shown below (Validate Drug Screen - Edit action):"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,160,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,161,0)="    Select Item(s): Next Screen// E   Edit  "
