^XPD(9.6,13560,1,526,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,527,0)="15.New option: eRx Holding Queue Processing [PSO ERX QUEUE PROCESSING] "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,528,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,529,0)="   This new option was created to replace the option Complete Orders from eRx"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,530,0)="   [PSO ERX FINISH]. The new option will have 100% of the functionality of the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,531,0)="   replaced option and some additional feature such as:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,532,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,533,0)="   a)Most of the prompts when entering the option have been converted into"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,534,0)="     User Preferences changed after loading the list and can be saved by each"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,535,0)="     user as their preferred View"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,536,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,537,0)="   b)The header part of the option was modified to display information about"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,538,0)="     the parameters used to compose the list, such as LOOK BACK DAYS, MAX."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,539,0)="     QUEUE SIZE, ERX STATUS, etc."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,540,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,541,0)="   c)The Grouping by CS (Controlled Substances) have a new format, which"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,542,0)="     separates entries in the queue."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,543,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,544,0)="   d)The user will be able to more easily switch views between the Patient"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,545,0)="     Centric and the Rx Medication queues via the PC and RX actions."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,546,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,547,0)="   e)Queue Search/Filter adds 3 new options in the Patient Centric View: RX#,"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,548,0)="     VISTA PATIENT and MATCH STATUS."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,549,0)="     In addition, the interface for performing searches was changed to display"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,550,0)="     information about the selected filters, including in the header part of "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,551,0)="     the list. The current filters can easily be reset via the RF (Remove"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,552,0)="     Filters) action."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,553,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,554,0)="   f)Queue Search/Filter adds 4 new options in the Medication View: RX#,"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,555,0)="     VISTA PATIENT, VISTA PROVIDER and MATCH STATUS."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,556,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,557,0)="   g)The MATCH STATUS filter was added to the Patient Centric and Medication"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,558,0)="     View and it has 4 different choices shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,559,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,560,0)="          1         PATIENT FAIL - PATIENT NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,561,0)="          2         PROVIDER FAIL - PROVIDER NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,562,0)="          3         DRUG FAIL - DRUG NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,563,0)="          4         BASIC - PATIENT, PROVIDER AND DRUG MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,564,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,565,0)="     1: Includes records where the patient has not been matched"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,566,0)="     2: Includes records where the provider has not been matched yet, but the "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,567,0)="        patient is matched"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,568,0)="     3: Includes records where the drug has not been matched yet, but the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,569,0)="        patient and the provider are matched"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,570,0)="     4: Includes records with the patient, provider and drug matched"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,571,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,572,0)="     Note: For a VA Medical Center site the list of choice will display "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,573,0)="           differently:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,574,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,575,0)="          1         PATIENT NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,576,0)="          2         PROVIDER NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,577,0)="          3         DRUG NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,578,0)="          4         PATIENT, PROVIDER AND DRUG MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,579,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,580,0)="   h)The header in the Patient Centric and Medication views will display"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,581,0)="     information about the selected filters, as shown below: "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,582,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,583,0)="     Rx Medication Queue       Jan 28, 2023@15:46:17           Page:  1 of  1 "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,584,0)="     LOOK BACK DAYS: 200       CS/NON-CS: BOTH (II-V)    MAX. QUEUE SIZE: 999"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,585,0)="     FILTERED BY: 01/08/23-01/18/23|PATIENT(TEST,PATIENT)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,586,0)="     _________________________________________________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,587,0)="     #   PATIENT              DOB      DRUG          PROVIDER    STA REC.DAT"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,588,0)="     ..."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,589,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,590,0)="     Note: The current filters can easily be reset via the RF (Remove Filters)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,591,0)="           action."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,592,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,593,0)="   i)Queue Sorting was streamlined to allow the user to quickly sort the list"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,594,0)="     through specific actions for each column and also allows for Descending"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,595,0)="     Sorting (not available in the replaced option)."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,596,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,597,0)="   j)The Change View (CV) action allows the user to reconfigure the way the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,598,0)="     list is displayed and allows them to save the configuration to be applied"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,599,0)="     to que queue when they re-enter the option."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,600,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,601,0)="   k)A new action called Refresh (REF) was added to allow the user to"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,602,0)="     re-display the queue. This feature allows the user view the latest"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,603,0)="     'locks' from other users that have been placed since the queue was last"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,604,0)="     built."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,605,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,606,0)="   l)A new action called Change Look Back Days (LBD) was created to quickly"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,607,0)="     allow the user to change the number of days to look back for records."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,608,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,609,0)="   m)A new action called Next Patient (NP) was created to assist users in"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,610,0)="     selecting the next eRx Patient on the queue to be worked on without too"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,611,0)="     many key strokes."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,612,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,613,0)="   n)A new action called Show/Hide Details (DET) under the Single Patient "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,614,0)="     list will show/hide additional information about each one of the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,615,0)="     eRx on the list. It will display Qty, # of Refills, Days Supply and the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,616,0)="     SIG (medication instructions)."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,617,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,618,0)="   o)A new action called Include All Statuses (IAS) under the Single Patient "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,619,0)="     list will show/hide non-actionable statuses like Processed (PR), "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,620,0)="     Removed (RM), etc. Furthermore, a field on the header will indicate"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,621,0)="     which statuses are being displayed: ALL or ACTIONABLE only."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,622,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,623,0)="   p)A new option is being added to the initial selection before entering the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,624,0)="     The new option is called Workload Processing (WP) and it is designed for"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,625,0)="     processing the current workload in a FIFO (First In First Out) method."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,626,0)="     Instead of loading a list of patients (PC Centric Queue) or Prescriptions"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,627,0)="     (Rx View), this option will automatically choose the patient with the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,628,0)="     oldest record to be worked on and will load it for the user to process"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,629,0)="     their prescriptions. Once the user finishes processing the prescription"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,630,0)="     for the first patient loaded they can choose the Next Patient (NP) action"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,631,0)="     to move on to the next patient. This option will use the ERX DEFAULT"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,632,0)="     LOOKBACK DAYS field (#10.2) in the OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) to"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,633,0)="     determine which one is the patient with the oldest record on file that"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,634,0)="     needs to be worked on next. The record must be in one of these 3 "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,635,0)="     statuses: New, In-Process or Wait."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,636,0)="     Additionally, this option allows the user to work on patients with"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,637,0)="     specific records that match the criteria below (see g bullet above for"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,638,0)="     more information on each filter):"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,639,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,640,0)="          1         PATIENT FAIL - PATIENT NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,641,0)="          2         PROVIDER FAIL - PROVIDER NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,642,0)="          3         DRUG FAIL - DRUG NOT MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,643,0)="          4         BASIC - PATIENT, PROVIDER AND DRUG MATCHED"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,644,0)="          5         ALL (NO FILTERS) "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,645,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,646,0)="   q)A new option was added to the Single Patient Queue: JB (Jump to"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,647,0)="     Backdoor). Instead of jumping to the Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMO"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,648,0)="     FINISH] option it will jump to the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,649,0)="     LM BACKDOOR ORDERS option."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,650,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,651,0)="   r)Within the Rx Medication Screen (or Rx List View Screen) the user will"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,652,0)="     have the ability to easily filter the list by Message Type by selecting"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,653,0)="     one of the following hidden actions."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,654,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,655,0)="           NEW  New Rx's Only"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,656,0)="           CR   Change Request Only           "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,657,0)="           RXF  Rx Refill Only     "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,658,0)="           IE   Inbound Errors Only "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,659,0)="           OE   Outbound Errors Only"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,660,0)="           CA   Cancel Rx's Only   "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,661,0)="           CN   Cancel Response Only"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,662,0)="           CX   Change Response Only"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,663,0)="           RRQ  Renewal Request Only "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,664,0)="           RRP  Renewal Response Only"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,665,0)="           ALL  All Message Types"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,666,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,667,0)="     Note: The same result can be accomplished via the SQ (Search Queue)"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,668,0)="           action and selecting #7 and then the specific message type."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,669,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,670,0)="   s)The NDC code will now be printed under the eRx Drug in the output print"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,671,0)="     from the Print eRx action, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,672,0)="         ..."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,673,0)="         ***************PRESCRIPTION INFORMATION******************"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,674,0)="         eRx Drug: MELOXICAM 15MG TAB "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,675,0)="         NDC: 00378108901"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,676,0)="         eRx Written Date: MAR 17, 2023      eRx Issue Date: "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,677,0)="         ..."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,678,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,679,0)="   t)The Remove eRx (RM) action will now work for eRx records that are "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,680,0)="     currently on Hold. Before, the user had to Un-Hold the record before"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,681,0)="     removing it."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,682,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,683,0)="   u)The Jump to OP (JO) action only allowed the user to 'jump' to Backdoor"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,684,0)="     Pharmacy option if the patient had pending orders to be finished. This"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,685,0)="     restriction is being removed by this patch."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,686,0)="      "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,687,0)="16.INC25762338 - Broken eRx drug auto-match on RxRenewalResponses"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,688,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,689,0)="   The ticket above will be addressed by this patch. This issue was caused by"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,690,0)="   PSO*7*706 released on December 12th, 2022. This patch moved the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,691,0)="   auto-matching functionality of provider and drug from the Hub to VistA. "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,692,0)="   However, the VistA did not implement drug auto-matching for "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,693,0)="   RxRenewalResponse records forcing the users to match the VistA dispense"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,694,0)="   drug manually. This patch will fix the issue by extending the VistA "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,695,0)="   auto-matching functionality to RxRenewalResponse records as well."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,696,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,697,0)="17.Routing field edit enabled for CS eRx orders"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,698,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,699,0)="   Users will now be allowed to edit the Routing (Mail/Window) field for a CS"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,700,0)="   eRx Pending order. Before, all field were un-editable in the OP Pending"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,701,0)="   Order Queue because an audit is not captured. However, the Remarks field"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,702,0)="   does not exist until created by the user in the OP Pending Order Queue."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,703,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,704,0)="18.New Pending Order side-by-side interface for eRx orders"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,705,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,706,0)="   Similar to the eRx Drug Validation screen shown above the view of a pending"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,707,0)="   order that originated from an eRx will be displayed differently in the "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,708,0)="   Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] and Complete"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,709,0)="   Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] options. When these option identify the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,710,0)="   pending order an eRx prescription it will automatically switch the display"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,711,0)="   of the data to a side-by-side viewing where the left side shows the eRx "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,712,0)="   prescription information (from the outside doctor) while the right-side"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,713,0)="   shows the VistA corresponding information."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,714,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,715,0)="   Besides displaying the information side-by-side, a few other features were"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,716,0)="   introduced to make the screen more user friendly, such as:"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,717,0)="     a) When there is a mismatch for field (e.g., Drug Name, Qty, etc.) the "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,718,0)="        content of such field will display in reverse video for both fields,"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,719,0)="        eRx and VistA."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,720,0)="     b) The content will display in highlight in order to stand from the field"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,721,0)="        label. "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,722,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,723,0)="     Obs) These features depend on the terminal display settings being set"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,724,0)="          differently for reverse video and highlighted font in order for it"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,725,0)="          to work."
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,726,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,727,0)="   Below is an example of how the new screen will be displayed (without the"
^XPD(9.6,13560,1,728,0)="   reverse or highlighted video features) for a new eRx Pending Order:"
