^XPD(9.6,13592,0)="PSO*7.0*729^60^0^3231205^y"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,0)="^^111^111^3231127^"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,3,0)="INCORRECT DRUG LINKED IN AUTOMATED DISPENSING SYSTEM FROM ONEVA"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,4,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,5,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,7,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,8,0)="1. INC27427008 - INCORRECT DRUG LINKED IN AUTOMATED DISPENSING "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,9,0)="                 SYSTEM FROM ONEVA"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,10,0)=" Duplicate: INC26949869"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,11,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,12,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,13,0)="Problem:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,14,0)="--------"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,15,0)="The original reported issue was that the drug matching logic "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,16,0)="forced an incorrect drug selection. The OneVA Rx sent dose for Nasal "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,17,0)="Spray. The pharmacist inadvertently accepted the bad drug with dose form"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,18,0)="tablet, likely because it was the only choice offered."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,19,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,20,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,21,0)="Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,22,0)="-----------"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,23,0)="This patch will enhance the drug lookup logic. The pharmacist will be "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,24,0)="presented with local Drug file lookup. Routine PSORRX1 is modified "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,25,0)="to mostly rewrite the DRUGMTCH subroutine."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,26,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,27,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,28,0)="Here is a list of requirements that are requested"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,29,0)="  1. If VA Product Identifier is received from HDR, the user is "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,30,0)="     presented with the message:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,31,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,32,0)="     Remote site VA PRODUCT IDENTIFIER: VA Product Identifier *** NOT"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,33,0)="     FOUND ***"""
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,34,0)="  2.  The VA Product Identifier that is returned from the HDR for then"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,35,0)="     host site drug item is used to identify the VA Product that the host"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,36,0)="     site drug is matched to. If the VA PRODUCT ID matches a product in  "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,37,0)="     file VA PRODUCT (#50.68) that is marked as a controlled substance in"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,38,0)="     field CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE (#19) (1-5), a message indicates that"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,39,0)="     Controlled substances are not allowed for ONEVA dispensing, and"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,40,0)="     processing stops."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,41,0)="  3. If there is a single drug match using the Drug name returned from "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,42,0)="     HDR and the VA PRODUCT ID, that is active, for outpatient use,"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,43,0)="     associated with a Pharmacy Orderable Item, and and not a "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,44,0)="     controlled substance in file #50, it is presented to the"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,45,0)="     user, with the prompt, 'Would you like to use the system matched drug"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,46,0)="     for this refill/partial fill? NO//' If the drug presented is not"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,47,0)="     accepted or there was more than one drug found that was a match,"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,48,0)="     processing will continue to step 3."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,49,0)="  4. Next through the ""APR"" cross-reference in the Drug File which is on "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,50,0)="     the PSNDF VA PRODUCT NAME ENTRY Field (#22) is used to find all drug"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,51,0)="     entries at the dispensing site that are matched to the same VA"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,52,0)="     Product as the host site drug selected for OneVA processing. "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,53,0)="     Eliminate any that are inactive, not marked for outpatient use, does"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,54,0)="     not have a Pharmacy Orderable Item or is a controlled substance in "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,55,0)="     file #50. Present the drugs and prompt the user to 'Select "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,56,0)="     drug from list (#-#) or <enter> to make a new selection:'"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,57,0)="  5. If no matching drug could be located, a drug wasn't selected or "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,58,0)="     no drugs were found, the user is presented the message:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,59,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,60,0)="         No other local match could be found for  DRUG NAME"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,61,0)="         You may need to update your Drug file to process this order"""
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,62,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,63,0)="         Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,64,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,65,0)="     NOTE: If no VA Product Identifier is received from HDR this message"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,66,0)="           will display after the message in step 1."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,67,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,68,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,69,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,70,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,71,0)="---------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,72,0)="Routine PSORRX1 is modified to mostly rewrite the DRUGMTCH subroutine."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,73,0)="Here is how the logic will function after the patch: "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,74,0)="  - Look for VAPID in ^PSNDF(50.68,""C"" index and "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,75,0)="    S VAPIEN=$O(^PSNDF(50.68,""C"",VAPID,0))"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,76,0)="  - Check if the product found in file 50.68 is for a controlled "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,77,0)="    substance. Using field CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE (#19). If the field"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,78,0)="    contains any value less then 6 and greater than 0, display message"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,79,0)="    and quit:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,80,0)="    S CSSCH=$$GET1^DIQ(50.68,VAPIEN,19,""I"")"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,81,0)="    I +CSSCH>0,+CSSCH<6 D  Q 0"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,82,0)="    . W !!,""Controlled substances are not allowed for ONEVA dispensing."",!"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,83,0)="    . D PAUSE^VALM1"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,84,0)="  - If the received VA PRODUCT ID is not found, display ""Remote site"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,85,0)="    VA PRODUCT IDENTIFIER: xxxxxxx *** NOT FOUND ***"" (processing will"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,86,0)="    quit out when VAPID not found after skipping over the )"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,87,0)="  - Then use DRGNM and loop thru ^PSDRUG(""B"",DRGNM) and save"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,88,0)="    any entries found into DRGARY(LDIEN) and increment counter DRLCNT.  "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,89,0)="    filter out drugs that are inactive, not for outpatient, not "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,90,0)="    associated with a Pharmacy Orderable Item, not linked to the VA"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,91,0)="    Product ID, and is not a controlled in file #50."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,92,0)="  - If only one product is found matching the above criteria, present "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,93,0)="    it to the user with the prompt 'Would you like to use the system"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,94,0)="    matched drug for this refill/partial fill? NO//'"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,95,0)="  - If the user answers Yes processing ends by returning the product's "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,96,0)="    IEN to the calling process."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,97,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,98,0)="The following are only done when VAPIEN exists:"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,99,0)="  - Loop thru the APR index of file 50 and filter out inactive, not for "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,100,0)="    Outpatient, not linked to Pharmacy orderable item, & not a "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,101,0)="    controlled substance in #50."
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,102,0)="    I '$D(DRGARY(LDIEN)) S DRGARY(LDIEN)="""",DRLCNT=DRLCNT+1"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,103,0)="  - At this point if DRLCNT>0, I send all matched drugs in DRGARY "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,104,0)="    (minus the drug already presented to the user) to ^DIR and prompt to"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,105,0)="    Select Drug from list (#-#) or <enter> to make a new selection:   "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,106,0)="  - If a drug is selected then ask, Would you like to use this drug?"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,107,0)="    If the answer is Y, then that drug IEN is returned "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,108,0)="  - If the user answers N or DRLCNT=0 after all the matching logic,"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,109,0)="    call SELECT and prompt to 'Select Drug:' and do not offer any that are"
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,110,0)="    inactive, not for outpatient use, not associated with a Pharmacy "
^XPD(9.6,13592,1,111,0)="    Orderable Item or a controlled drug (DEA Schedules 2-5) in file #50."
^XPD(9.6,13592,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
