^XPD(9.6,13636,0)="OR*3.0*603^35^0^3240208^y"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,0)="^^76^76^3240208^"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,1,0)="Description:"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,2,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,3,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,4,0)="1. In CPRS, the action of ""Change Release Event"" can be done on clinic"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,5,0)="medications."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,6,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,7,0)="2. In CPRS, Lab Overview (Collected Specimen) results are returned in "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,8,0)="wrong sort order by collection dates."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,9,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,10,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,11,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,12,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,13,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,14,0)="    the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,15,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,16,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,17,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,18,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,19,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,20,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,21,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,22,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter the patch name. "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,23,0)="        (OR*3.0*603)"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,24,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,25,0)="        NOTE: Using <spacebar><enter> will not bring up a "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,26,0)="              Multi-Package build even if it was loaded "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,27,0)="              immediately before this step. It will only "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,28,0)="              bring up the last patch in the build."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,29,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,30,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,31,0)="       a backup message. You must use this option and specify "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,32,0)="       what to backup; the entire Build or just Routines."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,33,0)="       The backup message can be used to restore the routines"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,34,0)="       and components of the build to the pre-patch condition."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,35,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,36,0)="         i.  At the Installation option menu, select Backup "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,37,0)="             a Transport Global."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,38,0)="         ii. At the Select INSTALL NAME prompt, enter your "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,39,0)="             build OR*3.0*603."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,40,0)="         iii. When prompted for the following, enter ""R"" for "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,41,0)="              Routines or ""B"" for Build."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,42,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,43,0)="               Select one of the following:"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,44,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,45,0)="                      B         Build"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,46,0)="                      R         Routines"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,47,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,48,0)="                Enter response: Build"
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,49,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,50,0)="         iv.  When prompted ""Do you wish to secure your build? "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,51,0)="              NO//"", press <enter> and take the default response "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,52,0)="              of ""NO""."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,53,0)="         v.   When prompted with, ""Send mail to: Last name, First "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,54,0)="              Name"", press <enter> to take default recipient. Add "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,55,0)="              any additional recipients."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,56,0)="         vi.  When prompted with ""Select basket to send to: IN//"", "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,57,0)="              press <enter> and take the default IN mailbox or select "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,58,0)="              a different mailbox."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,59,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,60,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,61,0)="         i. Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,62,0)="            you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,63,0)="        ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,64,0)="            option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,65,0)="            be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,66,0)="            all of the components of this patch, such as "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,67,0)="            routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,68,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,69,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,70,0)="       patch to install. "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,71,0)="         i. If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,72,0)="            Completion of Install? NO//', answer NO."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,73,0)="        ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,74,0)="            install? NO//', answer NO."
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,75,0)="       iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^XPD(9.6,13636,1,76,0)="            Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer NO."
