^XPD(9.6,13675,0)="RMPR*3.0*211^140^0^3240408^y"
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,0)="^^18^18^3221102^"
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,1,0)="The patch addresses two (2) issues: "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,3,0)="1.  When an end user attempts to reconcile the credit card charge to the"
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,4,0)="    purchase order using Reconcile/Close Out Purchase Card Transaction "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,5,0)="    option [RMPR4 CLOSE OUT], the application allows the user to delete "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,6,0)="    the last remaining billing item (original billing item) on the "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,7,0)="    purchase. If after the delete, the end user times out or enters an "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,8,0)="    ""^"" at Select ITEM, it leaves an incomplete record that cannot be "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,9,0)="    canceled or edited through the menu."
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,10,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,11,0)="2.  The option ""Purge Suspense Records"" [RMPR PURGE SUS] does not give "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,12,0)="    The user a chance to verify whether they want to proceed with the "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,13,0)="    purge. They do not have an option to cancel out of the purge once "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,14,0)="    the report is displayed, nor are they given an estimate of the date"
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,15,0)="    range that will be purged before they commit.  As a result, sites "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,16,0)="    are inadvertently running the purge or running it without "
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,17,0)="    understanding how much data they will lose.  This is causing sites"
^XPD(9.6,13675,1,18,0)="    to unintentionally lose important patient data."
^XPD(9.6,13675,4,0)="^9.64PA^664^1"
^XPD(9.6,13675,4,664,0)=664
^XPD(9.6,13675,4,664,2,0)="^9.641^664.02^1"
