^XPD(9.6,13727,1,96,0)="N/A "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,97,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,98,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,99,0)="============================================"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,100,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,101,0)="1. (HDSO-7262) New eRx RX CHANGE REQUEST user interface"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,102,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,103,0)="   The current eRx Change Request (EC) is being significantly improved to "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,104,0)="   facilitate the submission of RX CHANGE REQUEST messages to the prescriber."
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,105,0)="   Below is a list of modifications delivered in this patch: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,106,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,107,0)="   a)When the user selects the CHANGE REQUEST CODE D - DUE (Drug Use "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,108,0)="     Evaluation), they will be prompt to select a CHANGE REQUEST SUB-CODE as "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,109,0)="     shown below: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,110,0)="     . . ."
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,111,0)="        Select one of the following: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,112,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,113,0)="            D         DUE (Drug Use Evaluation) "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,114,0)="            G         Generic Substitution "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,115,0)="            OS        Out of Stock "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,116,0)="            P         Prior Authorization Required "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,117,0)="            S         Script Clarification "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,118,0)="            T         Therapeutic Interchange/Substitution "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,119,0)="            U         Prescriber Authorization "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,120,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,121,0)="      CHANGE REQUEST CODE: d  DUE (Drug Use Evaluation) "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,122,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,123,0)="        Select one of the following: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,124,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,125,0)="          AR - Adverse Drug Reaction "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,126,0)="          DA - Drug-Allergy "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,127,0)="          DD - Drug-Drug Interaction "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,128,0)="          DI - Drug Incompatibility "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,129,0)="          DR - Dose Range Conflict "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,130,0)="          HD - High Dose "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,131,0)="          ID - Ingredient Duplication "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,132,0)="          LD - Low Dose "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,133,0)="          MS - Missing Information/Clarification "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,134,0)="          PS - Product Selection Opportunity "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,135,0)="          SX - Drug-Gender "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,136,0)="          TD - Therapeutic "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,137,0)="          TP - Payer/Processor "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,138,0)="          UD - Duplicate Drug "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,139,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,140,0)="         Type '?' for the full list. "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,141,0)="     . . ."
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,142,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,143,0)="   b)The code G - Generic Substitution will always be available for selection "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,144,0)="     and in case the user selects this code for an eRx that already allows "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,145,0)="     substitution the following message will display: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,146,0)="     . . .       "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,147,0)="     CHANGE REQUEST CODE: G  Generic Substitution "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,148,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,149,0)="       Substitutions are already allowed by prescriber for this eRx.  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,150,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,151,0)="     CHANGE REQUEST CODE: "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,152,0)="     . . ."
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,153,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,154,0)="   c)A new field called NOTE TO PROVIDER will be presented to the user after "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,155,0)="     the code (and sub-code) is answered. It's a word-processing field and it"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,156,0)="     will be pre-populated for most codes/sub-codes selected with a "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,157,0)="     pre-defined template text. Some pre-defined texts contains place holders"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,158,0)="     such as [ADD_TEXT_HERE] and [DRUG_NAME] that must be replaced with the "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,159,0)="     actual information before proceeding.  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,160,0)="     . . ."
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,161,0)="     CHANGE REQUEST CODE: s  Script Clarification "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,162,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,163,0)="    =[ WRAP ]=[INSERT ]======< NOTE TO PROVIDER >=[Press <PF1>H for help]===="
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,164,0)="    The eRx is missing or unclear on [ADD_TEXT_HERE], Please edit and respond"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,165,0)="    or cancel Rx and send a new prescription with the requested information. "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,166,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,167,0)="    =======T=======T=======T=======T=======T=======T=======T=======T=======T="
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,168,0)="    Saving Text...  "
