^XPD(9.6,13727,1,286,0)="2. (HDSO-7263) eRx Holding Queue Display Conversion (Patient Summary "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,287,0)="    Display) "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,288,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,289,0)="   The new Single eRx View/Display option will replace the existing eRx "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,290,0)="   Holding Queue Display. The header will contain the following information "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,291,0)="   (without the reverse or highlighted video features): "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,292,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,293,0)="   Single eRx View/Display     Mar 04, 2024@15:49:40       Page:    1 of    3 "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,294,0)="   eRx Patient: LASTNAME,FIRSTNAME Y               eRx Reference #: 999998 "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,295,0)="   eRx Message Type: NEWRX "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,296,0)="   eRx Status: HC - HOLD DUE TO CHANGE "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,297,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,298,0)="   The eRx Hold Reason will be displayed on the first line or row of the "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,299,0)="   Single eRx View/Display list area.  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,300,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,301,0)="   Only display the eRx Hold Reason if it contains data. In the event that the"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,302,0)="   user put the eRx on hold but did not enter any reason, the eRx Hold Reason "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,303,0)="   will not be displayed.  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,304,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,305,0)="   Note: If the on-hold reason is longer than 60 characters, the eRx Hold "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,306,0)="         Reason will be truncated. The last three characters will be replaced "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,307,0)="         with three dots (...).  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,308,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,309,0)="   Within the Single eRx View/Display body/list area, the following will no "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,310,0)="   longer be displayed.  "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,311,0)="   * Hold Status "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,312,0)="   * Hold Reason "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,313,0)="   * Placed on hold by "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,314,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,315,0)="   a)If the message type is NEWRX, the display will be in a side-by-side"
^XPD(9.6,13727,1,316,0)="     format. Below is an example of the before conversion and how the new"
