^XPD(9.6,13805,0)="LR*5.2*573^14^0^3240917^y"
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,0)="^^13^13^3240605^"
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,1,0)="The patch addresses one (1) issue: "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,3,0)="1.      In certain situations, tests that are showing as collected do not "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,4,0)="have an accession number.  This happens when the user that accessions the "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,5,0)="test is logged into a division that is not defined in the LAB TEST FILE "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,6,0)="(#60) for that test with an ACCESSION AREA. When the user uses the option "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,7,0)="Accession tests ordered by ward order entry [LROE] there is a message "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,8,0)="that displays, but it is easily missed by the user causing lab tests to "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,9,0)="be presumed accessioned by the provider when the lab does not know that "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,10,0)="the order still needs to be collected and processed."
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,11,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,12,0)="When the order is accessioned by Howdy, no error message is displayed on "
^XPD(9.6,13805,1,13,0)="the screen and there is no way for the lab to know the order was needed."
^XPD(9.6,13805,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
^XPD(9.6,13805,6)="^472"
^XPD(9.6,13805,6.3)=7
