^XPD(9.6,13809,0)="MAG*3.0*350^175^0^3240926^y"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,0)="^9.61A^11^11^3240306^^^"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,1,0)="A problem was caused by patch MAG*3.0*226 (October 2019) which changed"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,2,0)="the way that Clinical Capture stored DICOM images."
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,3,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,4,0)="Instead of saving them as DICOM objects, they were stored as raw JPEG"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,5,0)="images with a *.DCM extension.  These images need to be converted to"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,6,0)="DICOM and stored as proper DICOM objects.  The previously stored JPEG"
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,7,0)="images need to be renamed using the *.JPG extension."
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,8,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,9,0)="These changes must be performed on both Tier-1 and Tier-2 storage."
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,10,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13809,1,11,0)="This patch corrects this problem."
^XPD(9.6,13809,4,0)="^9.64PA^2006.59935^1"
