^XPD(9.6,13919,1,120,0)="Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,121,0)="--------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,122,0)="The software for this patch is being released in a PackMan message."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,123,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,124,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,125,0)="Documentation describing the new functionality is included in this "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,126,0)="release. Documentation can be found on the VA Software Documentation "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,127,0)="Library at: https://www.domain.ext/vdl/. Documentation can also be "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,128,0)="obtained at https://download.vista.domain.ext/index.html/SOFTWARE. "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,129,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,130,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,131,0)="Documentation Title                             File "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,132,0)="Name                     "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,133,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,134,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,135,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,136,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,137,0)="Patch Installation:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,138,0)="-------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,139,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,140,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,141,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,142,0)="-------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,143,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,144,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,145,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,146,0)="------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,147,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,148,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,149,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,150,0)="minutes to install."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,151,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,152,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,153,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,154,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,155,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,156,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,157,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,158,0)="    the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,159,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,160,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,161,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,162,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,163,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,164,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,165,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,166,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,167,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter the patch or build name. "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,168,0)="        PSO*7.0*722"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,169,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,170,0)="        NOTE: Using <spacebar><enter> will not bring up a "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,171,0)="              Multi-Package build even if it was loaded "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,172,0)="              immediately before this step. It will only "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,173,0)="              bring up the last patch in the build."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,174,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,175,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,176,0)="       a backup message. You must use this option for each"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,177,0)="       patch contained in the Host File.  For each patch you"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,178,0)="       can specify what to backup; the entire Build or just"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,179,0)="       Routines. The backup message can be used to restore"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,180,0)="       just the routines or everything that will restore your "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,181,0)="       system to pre-patch condition."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,182,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,183,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,184,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,185,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,186,0)="             you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,187,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,188,0)="             option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,189,0)="             be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,190,0)="             all of the components of this patch, such as "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,191,0)="             routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,192,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,193,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,194,0)="       patch to install. "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,195,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,196,0)="      i.   If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,197,0)="             Completion of Install? NO//', answer NO."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,198,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,199,0)="      ii.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,200,0)="           install? NO//', answer NO."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,201,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,202,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,203,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer NO."
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,204,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,205,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,206,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,207,0)="-------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,208,0)="N/A"
^XPD(9.6,13919,1,209,0)=" "
