^XPD(9.6,14019,1,647,0)="12.Provider Auto-Validation for CS Drugs"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,648,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,649,0)="   The Provider Auto-Validation functionality released with patch PSO*7*700"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,650,0)="   (see item #5) will now be extended to digitally signed (indicating "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,651,0)="   Controlled Substance) eRx's as well. The only additional check performed"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,652,0)="   for auto-validating is that the VA provider must have a valid DEA# on file"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,653,0)="   that matches the DEA# sent with the eRx. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,654,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,655,0)="13.Ability to Un-Process VistA Rx with a DELETED status"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,656,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,657,0)="   Sometimes an eRx prescriptions that have already been transmitted to CMOP"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,658,0)="   must be un-processed so it can go back to the eRx Holding Queue. Therefore,"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,659,0)="   an exception was implemented in the software to allow non-CS eRx "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,660,0)="   prescriptions with a DELETED status to be un-processed even after they have"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,661,0)="   been transmitted to CMOP."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,662,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,663,0)="14.Allow Un-Accept and Re-Accept of Approved eRx Renewals"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,664,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,665,0)="   When a Renewal request is Approved by the outside prescriber the eRx will "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,666,0)="   got straight to the Pending Order without stopping at the eRx Holding Queue"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,667,0)="   first. The software will now allow the user to Un-Accept such records and "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,668,0)="   send them back to the eRx Holding Queue so an issue (e.g., Eligibility"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,669,0)="   verification, etc.) can be worked on there. Once the issue has been "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,670,0)="   resolved the user will be able to re-accept the record without having to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,671,0)="   perform any matches or validations."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,672,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,673,0)="15.Park Functionality in the eRx Holding Queue"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,674,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,675,0)="   The Park functionality released by the patch PSO*7*441, released back in"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,676,0)="   September of 2022 has now been implemented in the eRx Holding Queue. If the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,677,0)="   site has the Park functionality turned ON the user will be able to select"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,678,0)="   PARK as an option for the PICKUP ROUTING besides MAIL or WINDOW, as shown"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,679,0)="   below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,680,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,681,0)="    eRx Refills: 3"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,682,0)="    # OF REFILLS:  (0-3): 3// "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,683,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,684,0)="         Select one of the following:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,685,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,686,0)="              M         MAIL"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,687,0)="              W         WINDOW"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,688,0)="              P         PARK"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,689,0)="    "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,690,0)="    PICKUP ROUTING: M//"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,691,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,692,0)="16.No auto-match if Provider is inactive"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,693,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,694,0)="   A check was added to prevent an inactive VistA provider from being auto-"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,695,0)="   matched to the eRx even if the NPI matches. Furthermore, if the inactive"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,696,0)="   VistA Provider is a suggestion it will be automatically forgotten."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,697,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,698,0)="17.Patient, Provider and Drug/SIG auto-matching based on suggestions"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,699,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,700,0)="   The auto-matching functionality is being further enhanced to utilize "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,701,0)="   current VistA suggestions for Patient, Provider and Drug/SIG. For Patient "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,702,0)="   and Provider if no auto-match was found the software will look for any "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,703,0)="   existing suggestion and will auto-match to the latest VistA suggestion on"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,704,0)="   file. In the case of Drug/SIG it will be greatly improved by matching not"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,705,0)="   only the dispense drug but all fields from the suggested VistA Rx (if one"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,706,0)="   exists), exactly as if the user accepted the suggestion manually."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,707,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,708,0)="18.Updates to existing Accept(AC) action in Single eRx View/Display screen"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,709,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,710,0)="   The existing Accept(AC) action in the Single eRx View/Display screen will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,711,0)="   automatically try perform the validation (AV) for Patient (except for MbM),"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,712,0)="   Provider and Drug as well, if needed, before accepting the eRx. This"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,713,0)="   action will still perform all the checks necessary by each individual"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,714,0)="   record match and will display the result for validating each match"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,715,0)="   separately."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,716,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,717,0)="   Note: Please, refer to the user documentation for more detailed "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,718,0)="         information about this new functionality."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,719,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,720,0)="19.Ability to change the Hold code w/out Un-holding an eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,721,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,722,0)="   Users will now be able to switch the Hold code for an eRx on Hold for a"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,723,0)="   different Hold code without having to un-hold the eRx. Once the user"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,724,0)="   selects the Hold (H) action to hold an eRx already on software will inform"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,725,0)="   them the eRx is already on hold and will ask if they want to change the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,726,0)="   Hold code, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,727,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,728,0)="    Select Action: Next Screen// H   Hold  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,729,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,730,0)="    This eRx is already in a 'HOLD' status."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,731,0)="    Would you like to change the hold status and comments? NO// YES"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,732,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,733,0)="    Select HOLD reason code: HAL       NO PATIENT ALLERGY ASSESSMENT"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,734,0)="    Additional Comments (Optional): ASSIGNING CORRECT HOLD CODE"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,735,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,736,0)="20.First-In-First-Out (FIFO) processing for Complete Orders from OERR [PSO "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,737,0)="   LMOE FINISH] option"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,738,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,739,0)="   A FIFO order algorithm has been implemented for this option for users that"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,740,0)="   hold the newly created PSO ERX WORKLOAD RPH security key. Once the user "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,741,0)="   holding this key enters the option they will be prompted for the Clinic"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,742,0)="   they want to finish Pending Orders for and then if they want to process"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,743,0)="   Flagged orders only. After answering these two prompts the option will "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,744,0)="   automatically select the patient with the oldest record for the user to work"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,745,0)="   on. The user will not be able to move to the next patient unless all the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,746,0)="   current patient's pending orders are either finished or flagged. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,747,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,748,0)="   Note: Please, refer to the user documentation for more detailed "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,749,0)="         information about this new functionality."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,750,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,751,0)="21.eRx Prescriber Order Number in the Print"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,752,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,753,0)="   The incoming prescriber order number will be displayed in Print (P) under"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,754,0)="   the PRESCRIPTION INFORMATION section, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,755,0)="   ... "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,756,0)="   *************************PRESCRIPTION INFORMATION*************************"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,757,0)="   Prescriber Order #: ECWIA-9382026-211005-828"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,758,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,759,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,760,0)="22.Page breaking in the Print"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,761,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,762,0)="   The Print (P) action will now page break one page at time instead of"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,763,0)="   displaying the entire information, which forced the user to scroll up using"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,764,0)="   the terminal scrolling capability."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,765,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,766,0)="23.Allow Change Requests for eRx currently on Hold and Responses"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,767,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,768,0)="   Two changes are being made to the Change Request (EC Action) functionality:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,769,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,770,0)="   a) The Change Request (EC) action will be allowed to be run on eRx's that"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,771,0)="      are currently on Hold.  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,772,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,773,0)="   b) The Change Request (EC) action will be allowed to be run Response eRx's."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,774,0)="      Before, the EC action was restricted to the NewRx records only. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,775,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,776,0)="24. RxChangeRequest 'Therapeutic Interchange/Subst.' reason message templates"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,777,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,778,0)="   The CHANGE REQUEST CODE for 'Therapeutic Interchange/Substitution' has been"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,779,0)="   updated to allow the pharmacist/technician to choose a reason code linked"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,780,0)="   to a pre-made question template in the <RxChangeRequest> <ReasonText>"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,781,0)="   field. The user will be prompted to choose a CHANGE REQUEST SUB-CODE from"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,782,0)="   the options provided, as shown below."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,783,0)="   . . ."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,784,0)="       Select one of the following:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,785,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,786,0)="          D         DUE (Drug Use Evaluation) "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,787,0)="          G         Generic Substitution"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,788,0)="          OS        Out of Stock"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,789,0)="          P         Prior Authorization Required"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,790,0)="          S         Script Clarification"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,791,0)="          T         Therapeutic Interchange/Substitution"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,792,0)="          U         Prescriber Authorization"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,793,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,794,0)="     CHANGE REQUEST CODE: T  Therapeutic Interchange/Substitution"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,795,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,796,0)="       DSC - Days Supply Change"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,797,0)="       FMC - Formulary Change"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,798,0)="        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,799,0)="     CHANGE REQUEST SUB-CODE: DSC  Days Supply Change"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,800,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,801,0)="    ==[ WRAP ]==[INSERT ]======< NOTE TO PROVIDER >=[Press <PF1>H for help]==="
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,802,0)="    Pharmacy would like to dispense this medication for 90 days of supply"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,803,0)="    instead 30 days. Please approve the 90-days option below or Cancel Rx and"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,804,0)="    send a replacement."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,805,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,806,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,807,0)="    <=======T=======T=======T======T======T=======T=======T======T=====T>====="
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,808,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,809,0)="25.MbM Only: Auto-Holds for Pt. Eligibility and Non-Allergy Assessment "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,810,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,811,0)="   Upon arrival from the eRx Hub the eRx will be checked whether the VistA"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,812,0)="   Patient was auto-matched or not. If it was successfully matched, the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,813,0)="   software  will then check if the patient is eligible for ChampVA Rx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,814,0)="   benefit, if not, the software will automatically hold the eRx with an HEL "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,815,0)="   (PATIENT ELIGIBILITY ISSUE). If eligible, the software will then check if"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,816,0)="   the patient has an Allergy Assessment on file, if not, the software will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,817,0)="   automatically hold the eRx with an HAL (NO PATIENT ALLERGY ASSESSMENT)."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,818,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,819,0)="26.Menu changes to the Single eRx View/Display Screen "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,820,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,821,0)="   The bottom menu for the eRx Single eRx View/Display Screen was modified"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,822,0)="   to increase the listing area by 2 lines. Only 3 actions will be available"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,823,0)="   in the main menu: VD-VALIDATE PATIENT, VM-VALIDATE PROVIDER AND VD-VALIDATE"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,824,0)="   DRUG/SIG. The actions P-Print, RJ-Reject and UH-Un Hold eRx were move to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,825,0)="   the Hidden actions section, as seen below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,826,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,827,0)="   Main actions menu:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,828,0)="   -----------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,829,0)="     +         Enter ?? for more actions                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,830,0)="     "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,831,0)="     VP VALIDATE PATIENT     VM VALIDATE PROVIDER   VD VALIDATE DRUG/SIG"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,832,0)="     H  Hold                 RM Remove eRx          AC Validate & Accept eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,833,0)="     Select Action: Next Screen// "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,834,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,835,0)="   Hidden actions menu:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,836,0)="   -------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,837,0)="   Select Action: Next Screen// ??"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,838,0)="   The following actions are also available:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,839,0)="   +    Next Screen      Q   Quit                VO   View Original eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,840,0)="   -    Previous Screen  AD  Add Comment         VRQ  View Request eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,841,0)="   UP  Up a Line         ACK Acknowledge         VRE  View Response eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,842,0)="   DN  Down a Line       SH  Status History      REC  Resend Change Request"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,843,0)="   FS  First Screen      HL  View History Log    AC   Validate & Accept eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,844,0)="   LS  Last Screen       EC  eRx Change Request  H    Hold"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,845,0)="   GO  Go to Page        PA  Patient Allergies   P    Print"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,846,0)="   RD  Re Display Screen UR  Un Remove eRx       RJ   Reject"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,847,0)="   PS  Print Screen      JO  Jump to OP          RM   Remove eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,848,0)="   PL  Print List        UX  Un Process eRx      UH   Un Hold"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,849,0)="   SL  Search List       PN  Patient Progr. Note VSR  View Suggested Rx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,850,0)="   ADPL Auto Display(On/Off) AU  View Audit Log"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,851,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,852,0)="27.New View Suggested Rx (VSR) action"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,853,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,854,0)="   A new hidden action VSR was added to the eRx Single eRx View/Display hidden"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,855,0)="   menu. This option will allow the user to view the VistA Rx that was used"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,856,0)="   to suggest populate the prescription information for the current eRx. It "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,857,0)="   will invoke the same layout from the View Prescription [PSO VIEW] option."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,858,0)="   Once the user selects VSR and there's a Suggested VistA Rx that was used"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,859,0)="   to populate the eRx, the user will receive the following notice before"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,860,0)="   their are taken to viewing the suggested VistA Rx:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,861,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,862,0)="     Select Action: Next Screen//   VSR  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,863,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,864,0)="    _____________________________NOTICE______________________________________   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,865,0)="                                   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,866,0)="    You will be taken to the VistA prescription that was used to pre-populate"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,867,0)="    the Drug fields (Product/SIG/Qty/Days Supply/# of Refills/Substitution)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,868,0)="    for this eRx (aka, 'Suggested VistA Rx'). This VistA Rx may or may not be"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,869,0)="    for the same patient in this eRx being processed."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,870,0)="    _________________________________________________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,871,0)="    Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit:  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,872,0)="                                                                                "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,873,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,874,0)="28.New value for ACTION on SUGGESTION prompt: (V) VIEW RX"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,875,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,876,0)="   The suggestion prompt for the Drug/Sig will now offer a new option VIEW RX"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,877,0)="   (V) to allow the user to view the VistA Rx information before accepting it."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,878,0)="   If the user select V a notice will be displayed before taking the user to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,879,0)="   view the Suggested VistA Rx detail, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,880,0)=" "
