^XPD(9.6,14019,1,906,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,907,0)="29.VistA Prescriber Class displayed on Single eRx and Pending Order"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,908,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,909,0)="   The VistA Provider Class will now be displayed in the eRx Holding Queue"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,910,0)="   as well as when viewing an eRx Pending Order, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,911,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,912,0)="    Name: TEST,PROVIDER MD              |Name: TEST,PROVIDER              "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,913,0)="    NPI : 123456789  Phone: 9999999999  |NPI : 123456789  Phone: 9999999999 "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,914,0)="    DEA : XX9999999                     |DEA :                           "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,915,0)="    Clinic: Wellness Clinic Inc.        |Class: PHYSICIAN                "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,916,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,917,0)="30.New Next Drug (ND) hidden action"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,918,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,919,0)="   The Next Drug (ND) hidden action was introduced to facilitate the user "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,920,0)="   navigation to the Drug Validation screen for the actionable eRx from a "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,921,0)="   single patient. This new action will work from two different screens in the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,922,0)="   eRx Holding Queue:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,923,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,924,0)="     a) eRx Single Patient Queue: if the user types ""ND"" in this screen it "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,925,0)="        will take the user to the Drug Validation directly for the first "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,926,0)="        actionable eRx for the current patient."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,927,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,928,0)="     b) Drug Validation: if the user types ""ND"" in this screen it will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,929,0)="        take the user to the Drug Validation screen for the next (based on"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,930,0)="        eRx Received Date/Time) actionable eRx for the patient. If the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,931,0)="        patient has only one actionable eRx it will stay in the same eRx."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,932,0)="        If they current eRx is the last eRx on file for the patient it will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,933,0)="        loop back to the first eRx."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,934,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,935,0)="31.Indication functionality added to eRx Holding Queue"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,936,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,937,0)="   When matching the VistA Drug the user will now be prompted to also enter"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,938,0)="   the Indication. This functionality was only available in CPRS, Complete"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,939,0)="   Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] and Patient Prescription Processing"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,940,0)="   [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] options and it is now being extended to the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,941,0)="   Holding Queue Processing [PSO ERX QUEUE PROCESSING] option as well. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,942,0)="   If the patient record includes Indication, the user will now see the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,943,0)="   Indication shown on the Single eRx View/Display landing page."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,944,0)="   The Indication field will be displayed in the Single eRx View/Display"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,945,0)="   screen as well as in the Drug Validation screen, where it can be edited."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,946,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,947,0)="   Note: Please, refer to the user documentation for more detailed "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,948,0)="         information about this new functionality."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,949,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,950,0)="32.Added RRE and CRE error codes under CCR Filter"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,951,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,952,0)="   The two error codes listed below have been added under CCR Filter. This"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,953,0)="   will enable technicians to monitor and examine the RxChangeRequest/"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,954,0)="   RxRenewalRequest sent either by the VA eRx hub software or by the outside"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,955,0)="   prescribers."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,956,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,957,0)="   CRE RxChangeRequest Inbound Error      "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,958,0)="   RRE RxRenewalRequest Inbound Error"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,959,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,960,0)="33.Patient DOB check on Edit and Accept Validation warning"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,961,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,962,0)="   When editing or accepting validating the VistA patient, if there the DOB of"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,963,0)="   the eRx Patient does not match the DOB of the VistA Patient, the warning "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,964,0)="   below will be displayed:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,965,0)="     "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,966,0)="    Editing:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,967,0)="    *****************************   WARNING(S)  *****************************"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,968,0)="    Patient DOB mismatch (eRx: 01/01/1950 | VistA: 06/16/1936)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,969,0)="    *************************************************************************"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,970,0)="    Would you like to use this patient? NO// "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,971,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,972,0)="    Validating:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,973,0)="    *****************************   WARNING(S)  *****************************"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,974,0)="    Patient DOB mismatch (eRx: 01/01/1950 | VistA: 06/16/1936)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,975,0)="    *************************************************************************"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,976,0)="    Would you like to mark this patient as VALIDATED?"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,977,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,978,0)="34.Memorize the VistA patient when eRx is selected (<SPACE BAR>)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,979,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,980,0)="   When the user selects an eRx that has a VistA Patient matched to it, the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,981,0)="   VistA patient will now be memorized as the last patient accessed by the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,982,0)="   user, therefore when the user type <SPACE BAR> at a VistA PATIENT prompt,"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,983,0)="   it will automatically select the VistA Patient matched to the eRx."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,984,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,985,0)="35.HFF for Un-Accept and Un-Remove will now ask for Future Fill Date"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,986,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,987,0)="   When Un-Accepting or Un-Removing an eRx and selecting the hold code HFF "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,988,0)="   (HOLD FOR FUTURE FILL) the software was not prompting the user to select"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,989,0)="   a 'Future Fill Hold Date', which indicates when the eRx should be"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,990,0)="   automatically be un-held. This was causing the eRx to be unheld immediately"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,991,0)="   after being put on hold. This will be fixed with this patch."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,992,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,993,0)="36.IAS (Include All Statuses) action extended to Rx Medication Queue as well"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,994,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,995,0)="   The IAS action that was only available at the eRx Single Patient Queue will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,996,0)="   now be available in the Rx Medication Queue as well. This action is used to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,997,0)="   indicate that all eRx statuses should be included in the list and it will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,998,0)="   behave as such for the Rx Medication Queue as well."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,999,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1000,0)="37.eRx Prescriber Phone # displayed on Pending Order and Active Rx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1001,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1002,0)="   The eRx Prescriber Phone # will now be displayed for the eRx Pending Order"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1003,0)="   as well as for an ACTIVE eRx prescription."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1004,0)="   Pending order:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1005,0)="   -------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1006,0)="    Name: TEST,PROVIDER MD             |Name: TEST,PROVIDER              "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1007,0)="    NPI : xxxxxxxxxx Phone: 9999999999 |NPI : xxxxxxxxxxx  Phone: 9999999999"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1008,0)="    DEA : XX9999999                    |DEA :                            "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1009,0)="    Clinic: BFS - Gastroenterology      |Class: NURSE PRACTITIONER        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1010,0)="   Active order:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1011,0)="   ------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1012,0)="    eRx HT: (cm)()                  eRx WT: (kg)()                              "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1013,0)="    "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1014,0)="    eRx Provider: xxxxxxxxxxxxxx                          DEA: xxxxxxxxxx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1015,0)="    eRx Phone: xxxxxxxxxx                                 NPI: xxxxxxxxxx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1016,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1017,0)="38.VistA Drug Edit capability on the Single eRx View/Display screen"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1018,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1019,0)="   When viewing the eRx int he Single eRx View/Display screen the users will"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1020,0)="   now be able to edit the drug fields. Before, this capability was only"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1021,0)="   available in the Validate Drug (VD action) screen. This will allow users"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1022,0)="   to do quick edits such as Indication or Patient Instructions field without"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1023,0)="   having to go into the Validate Drug screen. The edit can be done "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1024,0)="   exclusively by typing the # of the field the user intends to edit, if #1"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1025,0)="   (Drug) is selected the user will be prompt to edit all other fields as"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1026,0)="   well. This sample shows #'s before each editable field:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1027,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1028,0)="      DRUG AUTO-MATCHED | VALIDATED by rrrrrrr   on 11/2/24@14:55:54"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1029,0)="   __________________________________________________________________________"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1030,0)="   Drug: Suprep Bowel Prep Kit 1.6 g-17|1)Drug: COLON ELECTROLYTE LAVAGE ORAL"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1031,0)="         g-17.5 g/177 mL liquid        |        SOLN KIT                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1032,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1033,0)="   Drug Form: LIQUID DOSAGE FORM       |        *** NON-FORMULARY ***           "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1034,0)="   Substitution? YES    Renewals? YES  |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1035,0)="   SIG:                                |SIG:                                    "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1036,0)="    354 ml orally 177 ml evening before| TAKE 1 KIT BY MOUTH EVERY MORNING      "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1037,0)="    and 177 morning of colonoscopy     |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1038,0)="   Prescriber Drug Use Evaluation:     |       Verb: TAKE                       "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1039,0)="    None                               |2)   Dosage: 1 KIT                      "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1040,0)="                                       |      Route: ORAL                       "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1041,0)="                                       |   Schedule: QAM                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1042,0)="                                       |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1043,0)="                                       |3)Patient Instructions:                 "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1044,0)="                                       |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1045,0)="   Provider Notes/Comments:            |4)Provider Comments:                 "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1046,0)="                                       |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1047,0)="                                       |5)Pat. Status: SC                       "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1048,0)="                                       |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1049,0)="   Quantity: 354                       |6)Quantity: 33                          "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1050,0)="   Dispense Unit: MILLILITER           |  Dispense Unit: TAB                    "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1051,0)="   Qty Qualifier: Original Quantity    |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1052,0)="   Days Supply: 1      Refills: 0      |7)Days Supply: 33     8)Refills: 11     "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1053,0)="                                       |9)Routing: MAIL                         "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1054,0)="                                       |10)Clinic: CWM/NO/PHARM/INBOUND ERX     "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1055,0)="   Written: 07/23/24  Effective:       |                                        "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1056,0)="   Primary Dx:                         |11)Indications:                         "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1057,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1058,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1059,0)="39.After AV it will go back to Single eRx View/Display (VAMC's only)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1060,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1061,0)="   A small change was made to streamline the processing of eRx's. Once the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1062,0)="   user accepts validation (AV action) for a patient, provider or drug, the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1063,0)="   software will take them automatically to the Single eRx View/Display"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1064,0)="   screen. This ways they don't have to type ""^"" or <ENTER>'s in order to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1065,0)="   go back to the Single eRx View/Display screen."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1066,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1067,0)="40.Default for Copy PATIENT INSTRUCTIONS from Rx#12345? Y// changed to 'NO'"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1068,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1069,0)="   When accepting a VistA Drug suggestion for an eRx, the software prompts the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1070,0)="   user if they also want to copy the Patient Instructions from the suggested"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1071,0)="   VistA Rx if it has this field populated. The default for this prompt was"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1072,0)="   'YES' and it is being changed to 'NO'."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1073,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1074,0)="41.Jump to eRx (JE) action modification at the Patient level"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1075,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1076,0)="   The Jump to eRx (JE) action used to jump from Backdoor Pharmacy back to the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1077,0)="   eRx Holding Queue is being modified to included all variations of the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1078,0)="   Patient that are matched to the same VistA Patient. Instead of jumping to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1079,0)="   the eRx Single Patient Queue the user will now be taken to the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1080,0)="   Medication Queue with the VistA Patient filter automatically set with the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1081,0)="   patient that was selected in Backdoor Pharmacy. Therefore, the list items"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1082,0)="   will include all eRx's from all eRx Patients that have been matched to the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1083,0)="   VistA Patient. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1084,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1085,0)="42.DEA Nightly Update Job w/ Data from DEA/DOJ"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1086,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1087,0)="   A new menu option called DEA Number Nightly Update with DEA/DOJ Data [PSO"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1088,0)="   DEA/DOJ NIGHTLY DATA UPD] is being created by this patch. This option is"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1089,0)="   used for automatically updating the Kernel DEA NUMBERS file (#8991.9) with"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1090,0)="   the latest prescriber DEA information from DEA/DOJ database. It will run"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1091,0)="   nightly and it will update DEA data for entries that are 30 days or less"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1092,0)="   from expiring. This new option will be added to the list of options that"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1093,0)="   can be edited via the existing Queue Background Jobs [PSO AUTOQUEUE JOBS]"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1094,0)="   option."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1095,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1096,0)="43.Patient address will ignore differences between similar words"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1097,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1098,0)="   The patient address comparison between eRx and VistA patients is being "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1099,0)="   enhanced to recognize and ignore these differences listed below by not"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1100,0)="   reversing the video if these are the only difference between the addresses:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1101,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1102,0)="      DR   =  DRIVE               APT  =  APARTMENT         STE  =  SUITE"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1103,0)="      AVE  =  AVENUE              W    =  WEST              S    =  SOUTH"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1104,0)="      ST   =  STREET              NW   =  NORTHWEST         SW   =  SOUTHWEST"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1105,0)="      HGWY =  HIGHWAY             NE   =  NORTHEAST         SE   =  SOUTHEAST"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1106,0)="      BLVD =  BOULEVARD           CT   =  COURT             RD   =  ROAD"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1107,0)="      TER  =  TERRACE             PKY  =  PARKWAY"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1108,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1109,0)="44.Conversion issue with Patient Weight when prescriber sent in g (grams)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1110,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1111,0)="   When the outside prescriber sent in a patient weight in grams (g) the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1112,0)="   software was not making the proper conversion to kilograms and it was"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1113,0)="   displaying the value in grams with a 'kg' indication in the Patient"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1114,0)="   Validation scree, as shown below:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1115,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1116,0)="          Weight(kg): 107161.2                   |Weight(kg): 107.95            "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1117,0)="          "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1118,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1119,0)="   After fix:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1120,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1121,0)="          Weight(kg): 107.16                     |Weight(kg): 107.95     "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1122,0)="   ..."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1123,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1124,0)="45.HFF (Hold for Future Fill) will now set the Effective Date if none"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1125,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1126,0)="   If an eRx is received without an Effective Date value and No Refills and"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1127,0)="   the user decides to hold it with a future fill date (HFF), if the date "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1128,0)="   entered by the user is more than 30 days from eRx Written Date the software"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1129,0)="   will set the Effective Date on the eRx with the future date entered by the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1130,0)="   user when placing the eRx on Hold with the HFF code."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1131,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1132,0)="46.CAO status will automatically be set with CAA (MbM only)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1133,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1134,0)="   When a cancelation is received from the outside prescriber and the eRx"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1135,0)="   status is set to CAO (CANCEL PROCESS COMPLETE) the software will "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1136,0)="   automatically set it to CAA (CANCEL REQUEST ACKNOWLEDGED) for Meds-by-Mail"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1137,0)="   sites. The reason is because the volume of CAO records at Meds-by-Mail"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1138,0)="   makes it impossible to acknowledge them manually one by one."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1139,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1140,0)="47.Cancelations of RxRenewal and RxChange were not DCing Pending/Active Order"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1141,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1142,0)="   When a RxRenewal or Rx Change response had been processed from the eRx "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1143,0)="   Holding queue and were either on the Pending or Active order queue and the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1144,0)="   outside prescriber sent in a cancellation for the renewal or accepted"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1145,0)="   change request the software was failing to proper cancel (DC) the pending"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1146,0)="   or active order for the corresponding medication. This issue is being "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1147,0)="   addressed by this patch."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1148,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1149,0)="48.Allergies compare between eRx and VistA were Case Sensitive"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1150,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1151,0)="   When comparing incoming list of allergies from the external prescriber with"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1152,0)="   the list of VistA allergies the software was performing a case sensitive"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1153,0)="   comparison. In other words, if the outside prescriber sent in 'Tomato' and"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1154,0)="   in VistA we had 'TOMATO' it would reverse the video on both because it"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1155,0)="   assumed them to be different. This issue is being addressed by this patch."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1156,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1157,0)="49.Update to the Pharmacist Enter/Edit [PSO RPH] option"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1158,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1159,0)="   Previously this option was used to allocated and de-allocate the PSORPH key"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1160,0)="   that identifies a user as a pharmacist on the system. It is now being "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1161,0)="   modified to allow allocation and de-allocation of the following eRx keys:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1162,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1163,0)="     PSO ERX WORKLOAD TECH "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1164,0)="     PSO ERX WORKLOAD RPH "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1165,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1166,0)="   These keys are mostly used by MbM to flag a user as a workload processing"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1167,0)="   technician or pharmacist, which prevents them from skipping orders, "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1168,0)="   effectively imposing a FIFO (First-In-First-Out) processing of incoming"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1169,0)="   eRx and Pending orders."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1170,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1171,0)="50.New option for Batch Change Request and VistA Drug Replacement"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1172,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1173,0)="   The new option Batch eRx Change Request/VistA Drug Replacement [PSO ERX "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1174,0)="   BATCH CH REQ/DRUG SWAP] placed under the Supervisor Functions [PSO"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1175,0)="   SUPERVISOR] menu option. It is used to perform two distinct tasks:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1176,0)="  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1177,0)="    Submission of Multiple eRx Change Requests"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1178,0)="    Replacement of the Vista Dispense Drug on finished prescriptions (MbM only)"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1179,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1180,0)="   The user will respond few prompts, specific to the task they want to"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1181,0)="   perform, a list will be presented before the user actually perform the"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1182,0)="   update. The Replacement of the VistA Dispense Drug is available to MbM "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1183,0)="   (Meds-by-Mail) only users. For more information about this option please"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1184,0)="   review the user documentation released along with this patch."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1185,0)="   "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1186,0)="51.eRx Pending Order Suggested FILL DATE auto calculation "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1187,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1188,0)="   Currently, the Fill Date field for an eRx Pending Order is always set to "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1189,0)="   the current date. In some cases this is not ideal because the patient might "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1190,0)="   still have enough medication to last a few more days and a future fill "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1191,0)="   date, based on the last fill for the medication might be more appropriate. "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1192,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1193,0)="   The algorithm will auto calculate the suggested Fill Date using the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1194,0)="   following logic: "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1195,0)="     Requirement: "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1196,0)="       - A previous prescription for the exact same drug must be found on the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1197,0)="         patient's profile "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1198,0)="       - The SIG from the previous prescription must match exactly with the "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1199,0)="         SIG for the new eRx Pending Order "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1200,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1201,0)="     Suggested Future Fill Date: "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1202,0)="       - If Last Fill is Released and the Release Date + Days Supply results "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1203,0)="         in a future date, this futures date suggested as the Fill Date for "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1204,0)="         the eRx Pending Order.  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1205,0)="       - If the CMOP Transmission status for the Last Fill is TRANSMITTED or"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1206,0)="         RE-TRANSMITTED, the Fill Date for the eRx Pending Order will be"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1207,0)="         today's date + Days Supply for the Suspended fill.  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1208,0)="       - If Last Fill is Suspended with a future Fill Date this future date"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1209,0)="         will be suggested as the Fill Date for the eRx Pending Order.  "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1210,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1211,0)="52.Added three (3) Remove Reason codes to the ERX SERVICE REASON CODES "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1212,0)="   FILE #52.45."
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1213,0)="   -----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1214,0)="   The three codes are:"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1215,0)="   REM81       Prior Authorization Denied"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1216,0)="   REM82       No Community Care Authorization for this Prescription"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1217,0)="   REM83       Patient Not Found in Local VA Database"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1218,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1219,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1220,0)="Test Sites: "
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1221,0)="----------"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1222,0)="Central Texas VAMC, Temple TX"
^XPD(9.6,14019,1,1223,0)="Meds-By-Mail"
