^XPD(9.6,14148,0)="EDP*2.0*42^212^0^3251105^y"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,0)="^^62^62^3251104^"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,1,0)="1) EDIS-1285: INC38814644 - EDIS Vitals saves incorrect time zone."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,2,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,3,0)="Problem:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,4,0)="--------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,5,0)="When adding vitals to a patient in EDIS the timestamp always displays "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,6,0)="central time regardless of where the site is located. This is because "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,7,0)="EDIS currently uses the time zone from the web server which is located in "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,8,0)="the central time zone."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,9,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,10,0)="Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,11,0)="----------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,12,0)="The current time was passed from the web server to VistA using Java's "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,13,0)="date/time method which would then store that value in VistA. Now the "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,14,0)="application does not use the Java date/time but instead uses VistA's "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,15,0)="$$NOW^XLFDT Application Programming Interface (API) call which will "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,16,0)="provide the time at that selected site. The time zone stamp on the vitals "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,17,0)="was removed in EDP*2*41 because there is no mechanism currently for EDIS"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,18,0)="to know what time zone the selected site belongs to."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,19,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,20,0)="2) EDIS-1348: INC39251650 - Tracking Code does not update in VistA."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,21,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,22,0)="Problem:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,23,0)="--------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,24,0)="When changing the name of the Status in EDIS under Configure > Selections "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,25,0)="> Status, the name updates in the Selections page and on the CPE screen. "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,26,0)="The new name of the Status does not update in the TRACKING CODE file "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,27,0)="(#233.1). The new name is also not visible in the Configure > Colors "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,28,0)="page. This appears to be an issue with all tracking codes -- dispositions,"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,29,0)="delays, etc."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,30,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,31,0)="Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,32,0)="-----------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,33,0)="When EDIS saves the updates on the Configure page the backend VistA code "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,34,0)="does not update the TRACKING CODE file. This VistA code has been updated "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,35,0)="to save changes to the TRACKING CODE file and to display the changes "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,36,0)="correctly in EDIS for any non-national code."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,37,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,38,0)="3) EDIS-1459: INC39876676 - EDIS creates duplicate encounters when a"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,39,0)="historical visit is entered in the ER clinic."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,40,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,41,0)="Problem:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,42,0)="--------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,43,0)="The site uses a Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) note as a warm"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,44,0)="hand-off when a patient is coming to the ER from another clinic or"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,45,0)="hospital location. The CPRS note is created as historical and linked to"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,46,0)="the ER clinic. This creates a historical encounter in the Patient Care "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,47,0)="Encounter (PCE) package. The note alerts the ER staff of the"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,48,0)="incoming patient. Once the patient enters the ER, the ER staff create an "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,49,0)="appointment for the patient putting the patient on the EDIS board. A nurse"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,50,0)="is assigned the patient in EDIS. EDIS checks the PCE package for existing"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,51,0)="encounters and finds the historical encounter. Encounter data (nurse "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,52,0)="assignment) cannot be added to historical encounters so a new encounter "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,53,0)="is created by EDPF Tracking System using the same date/time of the "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,54,0)="encounter. Now there are 2 selectable visits in CPRS, one for the "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,55,0)="scheduled appt and one for the EDIS created encounter. When users select "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,56,0)="the correct scheduled appointment and link their notes to it in CPRS, it "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,57,0)="creates a second encounter with the appt date/time."
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,58,0)=" "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,59,0)="Resolution:"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,60,0)="-----------"
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,61,0)="When EDIS is checking for a previous visit it will now ignore those "
^XPD(9.6,14148,1,62,0)="marked as ""historical""."
^XPD(9.6,14148,4,0)="^9.64PA^^"
^XPD(9.6,14148,6)="^36"
^XPD(9.6,14148,6.3)=6
